/-!
# `H¹(X, 𝒪_X(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1` on the blowup in a two-generated ideal

Let `A` be a Noetherian ring and `I ⊆ A` an ideal generated by **two** elements, and let
`X = Proj(⨁_{n ≥ 0} Iⁿ)` be the blowup of `Spec A` in `I`. Then

`H¹(X, 𝒪_X(n)) = 0`  for every `n ≥ -1`.

For `A` a regular local ring of dimension two and `I = 𝔪` this is part (2) of
[Stacks, Tag 0AGS]; the hypothesis that is actually used is only that `I` has two generators,
which the maximal ideal of a two-dimensional regular local ring does.

## The argument

The two generators present the Rees algebra as a graded quotient of `A[T₀, T₁]`, so
`i : X ⟶ 𝐏 = 𝐏¹_A` is a closed immersion
(`Stacks.Blowup.isClosedImmersion_blowUpSpecToProjSpace`) — and the target is a **projective
line**, which is where the hypothesis enters. Write `ℐ = ker(𝒪_𝐏 ⟶ i_*𝒪_X)`. The ideal-sheaf
sequence

`0 ⟶ ℐ ⟶ 𝒪_𝐏 ⟶ i_*𝒪_X ⟶ 0`

stays short exact after twisting by the invertible `𝒪_𝐏(n)`
(`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistFlatness.shortExact_map_twistFunctor_of_adjoin_degree_one`), and
the segment

`H¹(𝐏, 𝒪_𝐏(n)) ⟶ H¹(𝐏, (i_*𝒪_X)(n)) ⟶ H²(𝐏, ℐ(n))`

of its long exact sequence has both ends zero:

* `H¹(𝐏¹_A, 𝒪(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1`, by
  `Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.isZero_lineCohomology_one_of_neg_one_le` — the top-degree row
  of Serre's computation, over an arbitrary coefficient ring;
* `H²(𝐏¹_A, ℱ) = 0` for every quasi-coherent `ℱ`, by
  `Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt` — the projective line is covered by two
  affine opens.

**Nothing identifies `ℐ`**: only its quasi-coherence is used, which comes from
`Stacks.Blowup.isCoherent_kernel_projSpaceQuotientMap`. So the vanishing of
`H¹(𝐏, (i_*𝒪_X)(n))` follows, and two comparisons carry it to `X`:
`Stacks.Blowup.twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_iso` is `(i_*𝒪_X)(n) ≅ i_*(𝒪_X(n))` (the
projection formula at `i` together with `i^*𝒪_𝐏(n) ≅ 𝒪_X(n)`), and
`Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_of_isZero_Hgroup_pushforward` is [Stacks, Tag 089W] along the closed
immersion.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_one_twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_of_neg_one_le`:
  `H¹(𝐏¹_A, (i_*𝒪_X)(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_one_twistingSheaf_reesGrading_of_two_generators`:
  **`H¹(X, 𝒪_X(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1`** on the blowup in a two-generated ideal.
* `Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_of_two_le_of_two_generators`: **`Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `p ≥ 2` and
  every quasi-coherent `ℱ`**, the same transport applied to [Stacks, Tag 01XI] on `𝐏¹_A`. This is
  [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] part (1) on `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec`, for any two-generated ideal of a
  Noetherian ring; `AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le` is that clause on the
  relative-`Proj` model `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp`, for the maximal ideal of a two-dimensional
  regular local ring.

## Implementation notes

The blowup here is `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec I = Proj (reesGrading I)`, the ideal-theoretic model
over an affine base, and `𝒪_X(n)` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) n`; this is the model
both the closed immersion into projective space and Serre vanishing for the twists
(`Stacks.Blowup.exists_isZero_Hgroup_twistingSheaf_reesGrading`) are stated on.

Without the local transparency attributes of this file the sheaf of rings of `𝐏` is not seen to
be the one `AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj.twistSheafOfModules` takes its modules
over.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01XI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01XI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0C6K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C6K)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01E8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01E8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 089W](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/089W)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace
open AlgebraicGeometry
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj (twistingSheaf twistSheafOfModules)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjTwistFunctor (twistFunctor)
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistFlatness
  (shortExact_map_twistFunctor_of_adjoin_degree_one)
open Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology (polyGrading)

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] MvPolynomial.gradedAlgebra
attribute [local instance_reducible] ProjectiveSpectrum.top
attribute [local implicit_reducible] TopCat.Sheaf sheafCompose

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A}
  (x : Fin 2 → A) (hx : ∀ j, x j ∈ I) (hspan : I = Ideal.span (Set.range x))

/-- The generators of a two-generated ideal lie in the ideal. -/
private theorem exists_mem_generators_of_two_generators
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] {I : Ideal A} (hI : ∃ y : Fin 2 → A, I = Ideal.span (Set.range y)) :
    ∃ (y : Fin 2 → A) (_ : ∀ j, y j ∈ I), I = Ideal.span (Set.range y) := by
  obtain ⟨y, hyspan⟩ := hI
  exact ⟨y, fun j => hyspan ▸ Ideal.subset_span ⟨j, rfl⟩, hyspan⟩

/-- In a short exact sequence, `H¹` of the right term vanishes if `H¹` of the middle term and `H²`
of the left term do. -/
private theorem isZero_Hgroup_one_of_shortExact {Y : Scheme.{u}}
    {S : ShortComplex (SheafOfModules.{u} Y.ringCatSheaf)} (hS : S.ShortExact)
    (h₂ : IsZero (Hgroup Y.ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 S.X₂))
    (h₁ : IsZero (Hgroup Y.ringCatSheaf ⊤ 2 S.X₁)) :
    IsZero (Hgroup Y.ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 S.X₃) :=
  ((Stacks.DerivedIndexing.rightDerivedDeltaFunctorOfEnoughInjectives
    (secF Y.ringCatSheaf (⊤ : Opens Y))).scδ₁_exact hS 1).isZero_of_both_isZero h₂ h₁

/-- **`H¹(𝐏¹_A, (i_*𝒪_X)(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1`.**

`i : X ⟶ 𝐏¹_A` is the closed immersion attached to the two generators of `I`. The ideal-sheaf
sequence of `i`, twisted by `𝒪(n)`, has `H¹(𝐏¹_A, 𝒪(n)) = 0` on its left and
`H²(𝐏¹_A, ℐ(n)) = 0` on its right; the first holds because `n ≥ -1` and the second because the
projective line is covered by two affine opens and `ℐ(n)` is quasi-coherent. -/
theorem isZero_Hgroup_one_twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_of_neg_one_le
    (d : ℤ) (hd : -1 ≤ d) :
    IsZero (Hgroup (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (twistSheafOfModules (polyGrading A 1)
        ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I x hx hspan)).obj
          (SheafOfModules.unit (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf)) d)) := by
  have : Epi (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan) := epi_projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan
  have hse : (ShortComplex.mk (kernel.ι (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan))
      (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan)
      (kernel.condition (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan))).ShortExact :=
    ShortComplex.shortExact_mk_kernel_ι _
  have hseT := shortExact_map_twistFunctor_of_adjoin_degree_one (polyGrading A 1)
    (Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.SerreVanishing.adjoin_range_one_polyGrading A 1) d hse
  -- `H¹(𝐏¹_A, 𝒪(d)) = 0` since `d ≥ -1`.
  have hline : IsZero (Hgroup (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (twistingSheaf (polyGrading A 1) d)) :=
    (Stacks.Cohomology.CechAcyclic.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_Hgroup
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (twistingSheaf (polyGrading A 1) d)).1
      (Stacks.ProjectiveSpace.Cohomology.isZero_lineCohomology_one_of_neg_one_le A hd)
  have hunit : twistSheafOfModules (polyGrading A 1)
        (SheafOfModules.unit (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf) d ≅
      twistingSheaf (polyGrading A 1) d :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.tensorProductLeftUnitor _ _ _
  have hleft : IsZero (Hgroup (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (twistSheafOfModules (polyGrading A 1)
        (SheafOfModules.unit (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf) d)) :=
    hline.of_iso
      ((Hfunctor (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1).mapIso hunit)
  -- `H²(𝐏¹_A, ℐ(d)) = 0`: the projective line is covered by two affine opens.
  have hker : SheafOfModules.IsQuasicoherent (kernel (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan)) :=
    have := isCoherent_kernel_projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan
    isQuasicoherent_of_isCoherent _
  have hright : IsZero (Hgroup (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 2
      (twistSheafOfModules (polyGrading A 1)
        (kernel (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan)) d)) :=
    @Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt A _ 1
      (twistSheafOfModules (polyGrading A 1) (kernel (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan)) d)
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag0B5QUniformTwistBound.isQuasicoherent_twistSheafOfModules
        (polyGrading A 1) (kernel (projSpaceQuotientMap x hx hspan)) hker d) 2 (by omega)
  have h := isZero_Hgroup_one_of_shortExact (Y := AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)) hseT
  exact h hleft hright

/-- **`H¹(X, 𝒪_X(n)) = 0` for `n ≥ -1` on the blowup of `Spec A` in a two-generated ideal.**

This is [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] part (2) with its hypothesis reduced to what the argument uses: the
centre is generated by two elements, so the blowup is a closed subscheme of a **projective
line** over `A`. The vanishing is proved there — see
`Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_one_twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_of_neg_one_le` — and
carried back along the closed immersion by [Stacks, Tag 089W], the twist on `𝐏¹_A` being carried
to the twist on `X` by `Stacks.Blowup.twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_iso`. -/
theorem isZero_Hgroup_one_twistingSheaf_reesGrading_of_two_generators
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    (hI : ∃ y : Fin 2 → A, I = Ideal.span (Set.range y)) (d : ℤ) (hd : -1 ≤ d) :
    IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) d)) := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hyspan⟩ := exists_mem_generators_of_two_generators hI
  refine isZero_Hgroup_of_isZero_Hgroup_pushforward (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I y hy hyspan)
    (twistingSheaf (reesGrading I) d)
    (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.Tag0B5QUniformTwistBound.isQuasicoherent_twistingSheaf
      (reesGrading I) d) 1 ?_
  exact (isZero_Hgroup_one_twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_of_neg_one_le y hy hyspan d
      hd).of_iso
    ((Hfunctor (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj (polyGrading A 1)).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1).mapIso
      (twistSheafOfModules_pushforward_unit_iso y hy hyspan d).symm)

/-! ### Vanishing above degree one, and the globally generated case -/

/-- **`Hᵖ(X, ℱ) = 0` for `p ≥ 2` and every quasi-coherent `ℱ`**, on the blowup of `Spec A` in a
two-generated ideal. The blowup is a closed subscheme of the projective **line** over `A`, whose
quasi-coherent cohomology vanishes above degree one by [Stacks, Tag 01XI]; [Stacks, Tag 089W]
brings the vanishing back.

This is [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] part (1) on `Stacks.Blowup.blowUpSpec`, the form parts (2) and (3)
need. The same clause on the relative-`Proj` model `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUp` is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le`. The two models are identified:
`Stacks.Blowup.nonempty_over_iso_blowUpToBase` identifies `Stacks.Blowup.toSpec K` with
`AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpToBase` of the ideal sheaf `K` defines, as schemes over `Spec R`, for an
arbitrary ideal of an arbitrary commutative ring, and `AlgebraicGeometry.blowUpIso` identifies the
relative-`Proj` and Rees-sheaf models.

Transport along those isomorphisms would nonetheless not replace the proof below: the statement
here is for *any* two-generated ideal of a Noetherian ring, whereas
`AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_cohomology_of_two_le` is only for the maximal ideal of a regular local
ring of dimension two, so transporting it would give a strictly weaker result. -/
theorem isZero_Hgroup_of_two_le_of_two_generators
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    (hI : ∃ y : Fin 2 → A, I = Ideal.span (Set.range y))
    (F : (blowUpSpec I).Modules) (hF : F.IsQuasicoherent) (p : ℕ) (hp : 2 ≤ p) :
    IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ p F) := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hyspan⟩ := exists_mem_generators_of_two_generators hI
  have := hF
  refine isZero_Hgroup_of_isZero_Hgroup_pushforward (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I y hy hyspan) F hF
    p ?_
  exact @Stacks.ProjectiveCohomology.isZero_Hgroup_proj_of_lt A _ 1
    ((Scheme.Modules.pushforward (blowUpSpecToProjSpace I y hy hyspan)).obj F) inferInstance p
    (by omega)

/-- **`H¹(X, ℱ) = 0` for a globally generated quasi-coherent `ℱ`** on the blowup of `Spec A` in a
two-generated ideal: the first half of [Stacks, Tag 0AGS] part (3).

Global generation is a family of global sections whose morphism `π : ⨁_{i ∈ J} 𝒪_X ⟶ ℱ` out of
the free module is an epimorphism (Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`). Its kernel
sits in the segment

`H¹(X, ⨁_{i ∈ J} 𝒪_X) ⟶ H¹(X, ℱ) ⟶ H²(X, ker π)`

of the long exact sequence, and both ends vanish: the left because cohomology commutes with
direct sums on the quasi-compact quasi-separated `X` ([Stacks, Tag 01FF]) and `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0` is
`Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_one_twistingSheaf_reesGrading_of_two_generators` at `n = 0`, the
right by `Stacks.Blowup.isZero_Hgroup_of_two_le_of_two_generators`. -/
theorem isZero_Hgroup_one_of_generatingSections
    {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] {I : Ideal A}
    (hI : ∃ y : Fin 2 → A, I = Ideal.span (Set.range y))
    (F : (blowUpSpec I).Modules) (hF : F.IsQuasicoherent) (σ : F.GeneratingSections) :
    IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 F) := by
  have := hF
  have : Epi σ.π := σ.epi
  have hfree : (SheafOfModules.free σ.I : (blowUpSpec I).Modules).IsQuasicoherent :=
    inferInstance
  have hse : (ShortComplex.mk (kernel.ι σ.π) σ.π (kernel.condition σ.π)).ShortExact :=
    ShortComplex.shortExact_mk_kernel_ι _
  -- `H¹(X, 𝒪_X) = 0`, which is the twist vanishing at `n = 0`.
  have hunit : IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (SheafOfModules.unit (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf)) :=
    (isZero_Hgroup_one_twistingSheaf_reesGrading_of_two_generators hI 0 (by omega)).of_iso
      ((Hfunctor (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1).mapIso
        (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjEulerSequence.twistingSheafZeroIsoUnit
          (reesGrading I)).symm)
  have hsummand : ∀ _ : σ.I, IsZero (((Stacks.Cohomology.sectionsFunctor (blowUpSpec I)
      ⊤).rightDerived 1).obj (SheafOfModules.unit (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf)) := fun _ =>
    (Stacks.Cohomology.CechAcyclic.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_Hgroup
      (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1
      (SheafOfModules.unit (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf)).2 hunit
  have hleft : IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 (SheafOfModules.free σ.I)) :=
    (Stacks.Cohomology.CechAcyclic.isZero_rightDerived_evaluation_iff_isZero_Hgroup
      (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 1 (SheafOfModules.free σ.I)).1
      (isZero_rightDerived_sectionsFunctor_coproduct (blowUpSpec I)
        (fun _ : σ.I => SheafOfModules.unit (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf) 1 hsummand)
  have hkerqc : (kernel σ.π).IsQuasicoherent :=
    @Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QcohLimits.isQuasicoherent_kernel (blowUpSpec I)
      (SheafOfModules.free σ.I) F σ.π hfree hF
  have hright : IsZero (Hgroup (blowUpSpec I).ringCatSheaf ⊤ 2 (kernel σ.π)) :=
    isZero_Hgroup_of_two_le_of_two_generators hI (kernel σ.π) hkerqc 2 le_rfl
  exact isZero_Hgroup_one_of_shortExact hse hleft hright

end Stacks.Blowup

end
